 ### Verify a stored value through a second path
 
@@ -244,6 +244,10 @@ To test it, hold every transaction open after its read until all of them have ar
 
 For a call that changes another system, make the fake accept the request, apply the change, and then fail the call with a timeout. Run the retry. Assert that the work is still open and waiting for proof, not closed as "nothing to do". A mock that fails without applying the change cannot see this defect, and neither can a mock that always answers.
 
+### A setting meant to last for one transaction
+
+When code sets a session setting for the length of one transaction (a statement time limit, a schema search path, a role, a lock time limit), nothing fails if the setting is made for the whole session instead: the next caller on that pooled connection inherits it, far from the code that set it. Test it on a pool of exactly one connection: read the setting and the connection's identity before the call and after it, and expect both equal. The identity check stops a silent reconnect from passing the test. Then flip the scope by hand once and watch the test fail.
